<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David II of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1324">1324</a>–<a href="/years/1371">1371</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> II was King of Scots from 1329 to 1371, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a>. Driven into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-balliol">Edward Balliol</a> and the English in 1334, he returned in 1341, but in 1346 he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, was defeated and captured at Neville's Cross and was held in England for eleven years. He was released in 1357 for a heavy ransom and died without children.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-ii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="David II of Scotland" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scotland_penny_802002_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
